    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` checkpoint.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `Idempotency-Key` header now makes `POST /api/owners` idempotent: a repeat with an already-seen key replays the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate. I followed the codebase's established throw-and-handle short-circuit convention (the same mechanism `LoadOwner` \u2192 `NotFoundException` uses) rather than introducing flow branches.\n\n**New pipeline steps in `owners.POST.yml`:**\n- `checkIdempotency` (new first step, ungoverned) \u2014 reads the optional header via `ServerHttpConnection`, publishes it as an `IdempotencyKey` variable, and on a repeat throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the original owner, short-circuiting before any write.\n- `recordIdempotency` (after `audit`, before `respond`) \u2014 records the just-created owner's DTO against the key.\n\n**New Java classes:**\n- `function/common/IdempotencyStore` \u2014 singleton `@Component` mapping key \u2192 `OwnerDto` (survives across requests).\n- `function/common/IdempotencyKey` \u2014 typed wrapper so the key moves between steps as a distinct variable.\n- `function/owner/CheckIdempotencyKey` and `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 the two steps.\n- `escalation/IdempotentReplayException` + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` \u2014 replays the stored DTO with 200, plus its escalation YAML.\n\n**Key design choices:**\n- The header is read null-safely, so ordinary create requests (no key) are unaffected.\n- The store keeps the response **DTO** (mapped while the transaction/session is open), so a replay responds byte-for-byte with the original body and needs no database access \u2014 the replay path never opens a transaction.\n- The replay body is identical to the original create body; only the status differs (200 vs 201), so `extractId` reads the same owner id.",
