    "probe_text": "Read the whole pipeline. Here's the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes.\n\n## Guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is denied (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Ordered steps\n\n**1. `checkIdempotency` \u2014 `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(ungoverned, before the transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it as a variable.\n- *Validation / short-circuit:* if that key was already seen, throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the previously-created owner \u2192 replays it as **200** with no writes.\n\n**2. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`** *(transaction opens here)*\n- *Validation:* `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` runs bean validation \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`) on failure:\n  - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, letters with up to 2 space/`'`/`-` separators, size 1\u201330\n  - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, same pattern (trailing `.` allowed), size 1\u201330\n  - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, non-blank, size 1\u201380\n  - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, size 1\u201320\n  - `title` \u2014 size \u226410; `address` \u2014 non-blank, size 1\u2013255; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 size \u2264255; `email` \u2014 size \u2264255; `postcode` \u2014 exactly 4 digits `^[0-9]{4}$`\n- *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and republishes both the entity and the request DTO.\n\n**3. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` \u2014 `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`**\n- *Validation:* supplied `registrationDate` (raw, before defaulting) must not be after today \u2192 else `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n\n**4. `defaultRegistrationDate` \u2014 `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`**\n- *Side-effect:* defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent, then rolls Saturdays/Sundays/listed public holidays forward to the next business day; mutates the entity.\n\n**5. `normalize` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n- *Validation + side-effect:* normalizes telephone to E.164 (assumes `+61` when no country code, checks 8\u201315 digits and country-specific national length) \u2192 invalid \u21d2 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**); stores the normalized value.\n\n**6. `normalizeEmail` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerEmail`**\n- *Validation + side-effect:* if email present it must match the syntax pattern \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (**400**); lower-cases and stores it (no-op when absent).\n\n**7. `rejectDisposableEmailDomain` \u2014 `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`**\n- *Validation:* rejects emails whose domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n\n**8. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`**\n- *Validation + side-effect:* normalizes address (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand street-type abbreviations). Prefers structured `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`) and composes the flat `address`; otherwise normalizes flat `address`. Requires a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** flat `address` \u2192 else `InvalidAddressException` (**400**); mutates the entity.\n\n**9. `rejectInvalidPostcode` \u2014 `RejectInvalidPostcode`**\n- *Validation:* when a postcode is present, it must fall in the region range implied by the city (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n\n**10. `assignHousehold` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold`**\n- *Side-effect:* derives a deterministic `householdId` = first 12 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (null when no last name or postcode); mutates the entity.\n\n**11. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`**\n- *Validation (**409**):* scanning all owners (skipping soft-deleted), rejects an exact `identityKey` match, and rejects a same-`householdId` match **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set.\n\n**12. `rejectCityCapacity` \u2014 `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`**\n- *Validation:* if the (normalized) city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**13. `rejectDailyLimit` \u2014 `RejectOwnerDailyLimit`**\n- *Validation:* if \u2265 100 owners already share this owner's adjusted `registrationDate` \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**14. `assignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`**\n- *Side-effect:* unless `sharesHousehold`, if another owner shares last name + postcode but has a different phone, sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest such owner's id; mutates the entity.\n\n**15. `assignHouseholdSize` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `householdSize` = existing members with the same `householdId` + 1 (1 when no household); mutates.\n\n**16. `assignCustomerCode` \u2014 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode, HASH8 = SHA-256 over telephone+lastName), de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` on collision; mutates.\n\n**17. `assignNamesakeCount` \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive); mutates.\n\n**18. `assignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners already share the business-day `registrationDate`; mutates.\n\n**19. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n**20. `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`**\n- *Side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber).\n\n**21. `recordIdempotency` \u2014 `RecordIdempotencyKey`**\n- *Side-effect:* if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records the created owner's DTO against it so a later same-key create replays instead of duplicating.\n\n**22. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- *Side-effect:* sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body. The single transaction (steps 2\u201322) commits here.\n\n### Summary\n- **Validations (in order):** authorization \u2192 idempotency replay \u2192 bean-validation of the body \u2192 future registration date \u2192 telephone E.164 \u2192 email syntax \u2192 disposable email domain \u2192 address presence \u2192 postcode/region \u2192 exact & household duplicate \u2192 city capacity \u2192 daily limit.\n- **Side-effects (in order):** publish idempotency key \u2192 build entity \u2192 default/roll registration date \u2192 normalize telephone \u2192 normalize email \u2192 normalize/compose address \u2192 assign householdId \u2192 flag possible duplicate \u2192 household size \u2192 customer code \u2192 namesake count \u2192 bulk-signup warning \u2192 persist \u2192 audit log \u2192 record idempotency \u2192 201 response, all committed in one transaction.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the steps that reject on future dates, capacity, daily limit, and duplicates all run *inside* the transaction and scan `ownerRepository.findAll()` in-memory, so these checks are non-atomic across concurrent creates (TOCTOU) \u2014 but that's behavior, not something you asked me to change."
